#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:166
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of systemd"
msgstr "Instalação do \"systemd\""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><warning><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:171
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If a previous version of systemd has been installed, remove a service that "
"will generate errors on following boots. As the &root; user:"
msgstr ""
"Se uma versão anterior do systemd tiver sido instalada, remova um serviço "
"que gerará erros nas inicializações seguintes. Como o(a) usante &root;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><warning><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:175
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"pre\">rm -fv /usr/lib/systemd/system/systemd-update-utmp-"
"runlevel.service</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput remap=\"pre\">rm -fv /usr/lib/systemd/system/systemd-update-utmp-"
"runlevel.service</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:180
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Remove two unneeded groups, <systemitem "
"class=\"groupname\">render</systemitem> and <systemitem "
"class=\"groupname\">sgx</systemitem>, from the default udev rules:"
msgstr ""
"Remova dois grupos desnecessários, <systemitem "
"class=\"groupname\">render</systemitem> e <systemitem "
"class=\"groupname\">sgx</systemitem>, das regras padrão do \"udev\":"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:186
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput remap=\"pre\">sed -i -e 's/GROUP=\"render\"/GROUP=\"video\"/' \\\n"
"       -e 's/GROUP=\"sgx\", //' rules.d/50-udev-default.rules.in</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput remap=\"pre\">sed -i -e 's/GROUP=\"render\"/GROUP=\"video\"/' \\\n"
"      -e 's/GROUP=\"sgx\", //' rules.d/50-udev-default.rules.in</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:196
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Rebuild <application>systemd</application> by running the following "
"commands:"
msgstr ""
"Reconstrua o <application>systemd</application> executando os seguintes "
"comandos:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:200
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup ..                 \\\n"
"      --prefix=/usr            \\\n"
"      --buildtype=release      \\\n"
"      -D default-dnssec=no     \\\n"
"      -D firstboot=false       \\\n"
"      -D install-tests=false   \\\n"
"      -D ldconfig=false        \\\n"
"      -D man=auto              \\\n"
"      -D sysusers=false        \\\n"
"      -D rpmmacrosdir=no       \\\n"
"      -D homed=disabled        \\\n"
"      -D mode=release          \\\n"
"      -D pam=enabled           \\\n"
"      -D pamconfdir=/etc/pam.d \\\n"
"      -D dev-kvm-mode=0660     \\\n"
"      -D nobody-group=nogroup  \\\n"
"      -D sysupdate=disabled    \\\n"
"      -D ukify=disabled        \\\n"
"      -D docdir=/usr/share/doc/systemd-&systemd-version; &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd    build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup ..                 \\\n"
"      --prefix=/usr            \\\n"
"      --buildtype=release      \\\n"
"      -D default-dnssec=no     \\\n"
"      -D firstboot=false       \\\n"
"      -D install-tests=false   \\\n"
"      -D ldconfig=false        \\\n"
"      -D man=auto              \\\n"
"      -D sysusers=false        \\\n"
"      -D rpmmacrosdir=no       \\\n"
"      -D homed=disabled        \\\n"
"      -D mode=release          \\\n"
"      -D pam=enabled           \\\n"
"      -D pamconfdir=/etc/pam.d \\\n"
"      -D dev-kvm-mode=0660     \\\n"
"      -D nobody-group=nogroup  \\\n"
"      -D sysupdate=disabled    \\\n"
"      -D ukify=disabled        \\\n"
"      -D docdir=/usr/share/doc/systemd-&systemd-version; &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"ninja</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:228
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"For the best test results, make sure you run the test suite from a system "
"that is booted by the same <application>systemd</application> version you "
"are rebuilding."
msgstr ""
"Para os melhores resultados de teste, certifique-se de executar a suíte de "
"testes a partir de um sistema que seja inicializado pela mesma versão do "
"<application>systemd</application> que você estiver reconstruindo."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:235
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To test the results, issue: <command>ninja test</command>.  The test named "
"<filename>test-stat-util</filename> is known to fail if some kernel features"
" are not enabled.  If the test suite is run as the &root; user, some other "
"tests may fail because they depend on various kernel configuration options."
msgstr ""
"Para testar os resultados, emita: <command>ninja test</command>. O teste "
"chamado <filename>test-stat-util</filename> é conhecido por falhar se alguns"
" recursos do núcleo não estiverem habilitados. Se a suíte de teste for "
"executada como o(a) usuário(a) &root;, alguns outros testes possivelmente "
"falhem, porque dependem de várias opções de configuração do núcleo."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:244
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr "Agora, como o(a) usante <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:247
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>ninja install</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>ninja install</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:252
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr "Explicações do Comando"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:258
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D pamconfdir=/etc/pam.d</parameter>: Forces the PAM files to be "
"installed in /etc/pam.d rather than /usr/lib/pam.d."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>-D pamconfdir=/etc/pam.d</parameter>: Força os arquivos do PAM "
"serem instalados em /etc/pam.d em vez de /usr/lib/pam.d."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:263
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D homed=disabled</parameter>: Removes a daemon that does not "
"offer any use under a traditional BLFS configuration, especially using "
"accounts created with useradd. To enable systemd-homed, first ensure that "
"you have <xref linkend=\"cryptsetup\"/> and <xref linkend=\"libpwquality\"/>"
" installed, and then change <quote>disabled</quote> to "
"<quote>enabled</quote> in the above <command>meson setup</command> command."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>-D homed=disabled</parameter>: Remove um processo de segundo "
"plano que não oferece qualquer uso sob uma configuração tradicional do BLFS,"
" especialmente usando contas criadas com useradd. Para habilitar o systemd-"
"homed, primeiro certifique-se de que você tenha <xref "
"linkend=\"cryptsetup\"/> e <xref linkend=\"libpwquality\"/> instalados e, em"
" seguida, mude <quote>disabled</quote> para <quote>enabled</quote> no "
"comando <command>meson setup</command> acima."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:272
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D ukify=disabled</parameter>: Removes a script for combining a "
"kernel, an initramfs, and a kernel command line etc.  into an UEFI "
"application which can be loaded by the UEFI firmware to start the embedded "
"Linux kernel.  It's not needed for booting a BLFS system with UEFI. "
"Additionally, it requires the <application>pefile</application> Python "
"module at runtime, so if it's enabled but <application>pefile</application> "
"is not installed, one test for it will fail in the test suite. To enable "
"<command>systemd-ukify</command>, install the "
"<application>pefile</application> module and then change "
"<quote>disabled</quote> to <quote>enabled</quote> in the above "
"<command>meson setup</command> command."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>-D ukify=disabled</parameter>: Remove um conjunto de comandos "
"sequenciais para combinar um núcleo, um initramfs e uma linha de comando do "
"núcleo, entre outros, em um aplicativo UEFI que pode ser carregado pelo "
"firmware UEFI para iniciar o núcleo embutido Linux. Ele não é necessário "
"para inicializar um sistema BLFS com UEFI. Adicionalmente, ele exige o "
"módulo <application>pefile</application> do Python em tempo de execução, de "
"modo que, se estiver habilitado, mas <application>pefile</application> não "
"estiver instalado, um teste para ele falhará na suíte de teste. Para "
"habilitar o <command>systemd-ukify</command>, instale o módulo "
"<application>pefile</application> e, então, mude <quote>disabled</quote> "
"para <quote>enabled</quote> no comando <command>meson setup</command> acima."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:322
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring systemd"
msgstr "Configurando o \"systemd\""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:325
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The <filename>/etc/pam.d/system-session</filename> file needs to be modified"
" and a new file needs to be created in order for <command>systemd-"
"logind</command> to work correctly. Run the following commands as the "
"<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"O arquivo <filename>/etc/pam.d/system-session</filename> precisa ser "
"modificado e um novo arquivo precisa ser criado para a finalidade de que o "
"<command>systemd-logind</command> funcione corretamente. Execute os "
"seguintes comandos como o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:331
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>grep 'pam_systemd' /etc/pam.d/system-session ||\n"
"cat &gt;&gt; /etc/pam.d/system-session &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin Systemd addition\n"
"\n"
"session  required    pam_loginuid.so\n"
"session  optional    pam_systemd.so\n"
"\n"
"# End Systemd addition</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/systemd-user &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/pam.d/systemd-user\n"
"\n"
"account  required    pam_access.so\n"
"account  include     system-account\n"
"\n"
"session  required    pam_env.so\n"
"session  required    pam_limits.so\n"
"session  required    pam_loginuid.so\n"
"session  optional    pam_keyinit.so force revoke\n"
"session  optional    pam_systemd.so\n"
"\n"
"auth     required    pam_deny.so\n"
"password required    pam_deny.so\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/pam.d/systemd-user</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>grep 'pam_systemd' /etc/pam.d/system-session ||\n"
"cat &gt;&gt; /etc/pam.d/system-session &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Inicia adições do Systemd\n"
"\n"
"session  required    pam_loginuid.so\n"
"session  optional    pam_systemd.so\n"
"\n"
"# Termina adições do Systemd</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/pam.d/systemd-user &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Inicia /etc/pam.d/systemd-user\n"
"\n"
"account  required    pam_access.so\n"
"account  include     system-account\n"
"\n"
"session  required    pam_env.so\n"
"session  required    pam_limits.so\n"
"session  required    pam_loginuid.so\n"
"session  optional    pam_keyinit.so force revoke\n"
"session  optional    pam_systemd.so\n"
"\n"
"auth     required    pam_deny.so\n"
"password required    pam_deny.so\n"
"\n"
"# Termina /etc/pam.d/systemd-user</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:366
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"As the &root; user, replace the running <command>systemd</command> manager "
"(the <command>init</command> process) with the <command>systemd</command> "
"executable newly built and installed:"
msgstr ""
"Como o(a) usuário(a) &root;, substitua o gerenciador "
"<command>systemd</command> em execução (o processo <command>init</command>) "
"pelo executável <command>systemd</command> recém-construído e instalado:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:371
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>systemctl daemon-reexec</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>systemctl daemon-reexec</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:374
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"A desktop environment often runs as a group of systemd user services.  Those"
" services are spawned by the systemd per-user instance, instead of the login"
" shell.  To ensure those services get the environment variables we've set "
"via <filename class='directory'>/etc/profile.d</filename>, as the &root; "
"user, install a systemd environment generator to dump all the relevant "
"exported environment variables into the systemd per-user instance when the "
"instance starts to run:"
msgstr ""
"Um ambiente de área de trabalho frequentemente executa como um grupo de "
"serviços de usuário(a) do systemd. Esses serviços são gerados pela instância"
" por usuário(a) do systemd, em vez do shell de login. Para garantir que "
"esses serviços obtenham as variáveis de ambiente que nós configuramos via "
"<filename class='directory'>/etc/profile.d</filename>; como o(a) usuário(a) "
"&root;, instale um gerador de ambiente do systemd para despejar todas as "
"variáveis de ambiente exportadas relevantes na instância por usuário(a) do "
"systemd quando a instância iniciar para executar:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:384
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>install -vdm755 /etc/systemd/user-environment-generators &amp;&amp;\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/systemd/user-environment-generators/50-profile.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal>#!/usr/bin/env -S -i /usr/bin/bash\n"
"# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n"
"\n"
". /etc/profile\n"
"\n"
"# Systemd should have already set a better value for them.\n"
"unset XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\n"
"for i in $(locale); do\n"
"  unset ${i%=*}\n"
"done\n"
"\n"
"# Some shell magic that we don't want to expose.\n"
"unset SHLVL\n"
"\n"
"# Systemd does not want to pass functions to the environment\n"
"for i in $(declare -pF | awk '{print $3}'); do\n"
"  unset -f $i\n"
"done\n"
"\n"
"python3 &lt;&lt; _EOF\n"
"import os\n"
"for var in os.environ:\n"
"  # Simply unsetting them in shell does not work.\n"
"  if var in ['LC_CTYPE', '_']:\n"
"    continue\n"
"\n"
"  print(var + '=' + os.environ[var])\n"
"_EOF</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"chmod -v 755 /etc/systemd/user-environment-generators/50-profile.sh</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>install -vdm755 /etc/systemd/user-environment-generators &amp;&amp;\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/systemd/user-environment-generators/50-profile.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\" &amp;&amp;\n"
"<literal>#!/usr/bin/env -S -i /usr/bin/bash\n"
"# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n"
"\n"
". /etc/profile\n"
"\n"
"# Systemd should have already set a better value for them.\n"
"unset XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\n"
"for i in $(locale); do\n"
"  unset ${i%=*}\n"
"done\n"
"\n"
"# Some shell magic that we don't want to expose.\n"
"unset SHLVL\n"
"\n"
"# Systemd does not want to pass functions to the environment\n"
"for i in $(declare -pF | awk '{print $3}'); do\n"
"  unset -f $i\n"
"done\n"
"\n"
"python3 &lt;&lt; _EOF\n"
"import os\n"
"for var in os.environ:\n"
"  # Simply unsetting them in shell does not work.\n"
"  if var in ['LC_CTYPE', '_']:\n"
"    continue\n"
"\n"
"  print(var + '=' + os.environ[var])\n"
"_EOF</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"chmod -v 755 /etc/systemd/user-environment-generators/50-profile.sh</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:419
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Read <ulink role='man' url='&man;systemd.environment-"
"generator.7'>systemd.environment-generator(7)</ulink> for details about the "
"systemd environment generators.  Note that if you've edited the content of "
"<filename class='directory'>/etc/profile.d</filename> when a desktop "
"environment is running, you need to sync the change into the systemd per-"
"user instance:"
msgstr ""
"Leia-se <ulink role='man' url='&man;systemd.environment-"
"generator.7'>systemd.environment-generator(7)</ulink> para detalhes acerca "
"dos geradores de ambiente do systemd. Observe que se tiver editado o "
"conteúdo de <filename class='directory'>/etc/profile.d</filename> quando um "
"ambiente de área de trabalho estiver executando, você precisará sincronizar "
"a mudança na instância systemd por usuário(a):"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:428
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>systemctl --user unset-environment \\\n"
"  $(/etc/systemd/user-environment-generators/50-profile.sh | sed 's/=.*//')\n"
"systemctl --user daemon-reload</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>systemctl --user unset-environment \\\n"
"  $(/etc/systemd/user-environment-generators/50-profile.sh | sed 's/=.*//')\n"
"systemctl --user daemon-reload</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:433
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"And then log out and log in again to sync the change into the desktop "
"environment.  The <command>systemctl --user unset-environment</command> "
"command is needed on some desktop environments which write the environment "
"variables into the runtime environment variable pool of the per-user systemd"
" instance because the content of that pool would override the setting from "
"the generator."
msgstr ""
"E, em seguida, deslogar-se e logar-se novamente para sincronizar a mudança "
"no ambiente de área de trabalho. O comando <command>systemctl --user unset-"
"environment</command> é necessário em alguns ambientes de área de trabalho "
"que escrevam as variáveis de ambiente no bloco de variáveis de ambiente em "
"tempo de execução da instância systemd por usuário(a), porque o conteúdo "
"desse bloco de variáveis substituiria a configuração proveniente do gerador."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><important><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:444
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Now ensure <xref linkend='shadow'/> has been already rebuilt with <xref "
"linkend='linux-pam'/> support first, then logout, and login again. This will"
" ensure that the running login session is registered with <command>systemd-"
"logind</command>, and that a per-user systemd instance is running for each "
"user owning a login session. Many BLFS packages listing systemd as a "
"dependency need the <command>systemd-logind</command> integration and/or a "
"running per-user systemd instance at runtime."
msgstr ""
"Agora certifique-se de que <xref linkend='shadow'/> já tenha sido "
"reconstruído com suporte <xref linkend='linux-pam'/> primeiro, depois "
"deslogue-se e logue-se novamente. Isso garantirá que a sessão de login em "
"execução seja registrada com <command>systemd-logind</command> e que uma "
"instância do systemd por usuário(a) esteja executando para cada usuário(a) "
"titularizando uma sessão de login. Muitos pacotes do BLFS que listam o "
"systemd como uma dependência precisam da integração do <command>systemd-"
"logind</command> e (ou) de uma instância do systemd em execução por "
"usuário(a) em tempo de execução."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><warning><para>
#: blfs-en/general/sysutils/systemd.xml:457
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you are upgrading from a previous version of systemd and an initrd is "
"used for system boot, you should generate a new initrd before rebooting the "
"system."
msgstr ""
"Se estiver atualizando a partir de uma versão anterior do systemd e um "
"initrd for usado para inicialização do sistema, você deveria gerar um novo "
"initrd antes de reinicializar o sistema."

